      "claim": "The use of nuclear weapons constitutes a war crime because they are weapons that are inherently indiscriminate and cause superfluous injury or unnecessary suffering.",
      "reasoning": "Article 8 of the Rome Statute criminalises the employment of weapons \"of a nature to cause superfluous injury or unnecessary suffering or which are inherently indiscriminate\". Nuclear weapons, by their very design, cannot be directed at a specific target without affecting civilians and cause injuries far beyond what is necessary to achieve a military objective, satisfying the elements of the prohibited category.",
