      "claim": "The use of nuclear weapons is unlawful because it causes extensive, long‑term and severe damage to the natural environment that is clearly excessive in relation to any concrete and direct military advantage.",
      "reasoning": "Article 8(b)(iv) of the Rome Statute prohibits \"intentionally launching an attack ... which will cause ... widespread, long‑term and severe damage to the natural environment which would be clearly excessive in relation to the concrete and direct overall military advantage anticipated\". The radiological fallout, contamination of land, water and air, and inter‑generational health effects of nuclear weapons meet this description, making such attacks unlawful regardless of the self‑defence context.",
